📊 Conditional Formatting in Excel for Data & Business Analytics
📌 Overview
This learning session focused on **Conditional Formatting in Advanced Excel** and how Data Analysts and Business Analysts can use visual rules to quickly identify important patterns, exceptions, trends, and performance differences within business datasets.

Conditional Formatting is more than changing cell colors. When used correctly, it helps transform:

Raw Data → Visual Signals → Faster Analysis → Business Insights → Better Decisions

---
🎯 Topics Covered

* Highlight high, low, and exact values
* Identify top & bottom performers
* Compare values against averages
* Data Bars
* Color Scales
* Icon Sets
* Text-based Conditional Formatting
* Formula-driven rules
* Highlight entire rows
* Combine multiple rules
* Manage rule priority
* Apply Conditional Formatting to business datasets

